    "done_when": "watch.watch_text and watch.watch_document (the text and --json paths) no longer call discover() or TelemetryIndex.ingest; they open the index through a new read-only constructor on TelemetryIndex that opens the file with a SQLite URI in mode=ro and a 5 s busy timeout, never creates the file or its parent directory, and never runs the schema script or a migration; with no file at the index path the text output states that no index exists at that path and that the fleet's ingest service (imas-ambix agent ingest) maintains it, prints no period or ledger rows, and the --json document carries index.exists false with the path and no period rows; with a file present both outputs show the index's last-ingest time, taken as the file's modification time in UTC to the second, with its age, the --json document carrying index.path, index.exists true, index.last_ingest_at and index.age_seconds; --live is unchanged; tests in tests/test_agent_telemetry_watch.py assert that a watch call over a fixture index whose receipts directory holds a source never ingested leaves the index's sample count and file bytes unchanged, that a missing index is reported and not created (the path and its parent directory still absent afterwards), that last_ingest_at equals a literal set through os.utime, and that the read-only handle refuses an INSERT with sqlite3.OperationalError; existing watch tests that relied on ingest-on-read now ingest in their fixture setup through TelemetryIndex.ingest; gate: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_agent_telemetry_watch.py tests/test_agent_watch_live.py tests/test_agent_watch_cost.py tests/test_agent_watch_help.py tests/test_telemetry_index.py passes, pytest tests/test_agent_serve_registry.py -k agent_package_modules_parse_with_serving_python passes, uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0; the gate log's first line names the commit it ran at and each command's exit status is recorded as EXIT=0 or the non-zero status",
